WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
We were always very close to the priest.

2
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:10.840
They would always come over to eat on Sundays with us and everything.

3
00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:17.380
I’m glad you asked about the dynamic of the church because I always had a problem with the church.

4
00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:23.500
Simply because . . . And it’s still that way today: when you walk in,

5
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.100
there’s a black side of the church and a white side of the church.

6
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.260
My daddy was always a rebel.

7
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.040
So we sat on the white side.

8
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:36.220
And the graveyard is separated by the black side and the white side.

9
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:41.080
My daddy is buried on the white side.

10
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:41.560
Yeah.

11
00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:49.560
That’s what . . . My parents are the only two blacks buried on the opposite side of the graveyard.

12
00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.180
He just wasn’t having it.

13
00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.760
He was an activist.

14
00:00:54.760 --> 00:01:03.700
I don’t know how that got instilled in him to be that way, but he wasn’t having it.

15
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:05.280
I look out on the congregation,

16
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:14.960
and I always wondered how can a priest look out on the congregation on a regular basis and see the people,

17
00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:19.160
the parishioners, divided that way and not ever speak on it?

18
00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:20.580
Not ever say anything.

19
00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.220
That’s why I had a problem with it.

20
00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.580
That’s why I didn’t mind going to church at school, because it wasn’t that way.

21
00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:35.160
I was only one of nine blacks, but still, you know, you didn’t feel like you didn’t belong.

22
00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.220
And it just felt strange.
